Hi Sam,

Without running the code.. what exactly is the problem? It won't converge or is sensitive to starting values? Convergence but non-invertible Hessian? Previous threads discussed that those NaN warnings can be normal for stable models as well, so they don't necessarily indicate an issue.

Instead of a grid search you could try turning off estimation of parameters with map until the behavior disappears? Then slowly add complexity back in.

If you think the model may have insufficient data then you could easily test this by putting mildly informative priors on parameters and see if the problem clears up. Alternatively you could try running it through tmbstan  <http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0197954>and see if the NUTS sampler helps identifies issues (via divergences or large tree depths).

Cheers,
Cole

